  "prediction": "**Deadly Shooting on Las Vegas Strip Leaves Three Dead and Six Injured**\n\nA violent shooting on the Las Vegas Strip early Thursday morning left three people dead and at least six injured. The incident occurred when a black Range Rover SUV opened fire on a Maserati, causing it to crash into a taxi that burst into flames. The taxi driver, Michael Boldon, and two others were killed in the incident.\n\nAccording to police, the shooting was sparked by an altercation at a nearby hotel, which spilled onto the streets. The vehicles involved in the dispute were a silver-gray Maserati and a black Range Rover SUV. The Maserati sped off at a high rate of speed, and the SUV followed, firing gunshots at the Maserati. The Maserati then crashed into a taxi, which exploded in a fireball.\n\nThe driver of the Maserati, identified as Kenneth Wayne Cherry Jr., 27, was pronounced dead at a hospital. A passenger in the Maserati was among the injured. The SUV, which was seen fleeing the scene, is still at large, and authorities have contacted police in three neighboring states to be on the lookout for the vehicle.\n\nThe incident has raised concerns about safety on the Las Vegas Strip, which is known for its high level of security. However, police have assured tourists that the area is still safe and that the incident was an isolated event.\n\n**Investigation and Aftermath**\n\nPolice are still investigating the incident and have collected video from traffic cameras at the intersection. They are also checking hotel surveillance systems to determine the cause of the altercation. The police have identified several people who were in the SUV, but it is not clear if they were involved in the shooting.\n\nThe incident has sparked an outpouring of support for the victims and their families. A taxi driver organization has donated $5,000 to the Boldon family, and several people have expressed their condolences on social media.\n\n**Recent Violence on the Strip**\n\nThe incident is the latest in a series of violent incidents on the Las Vegas Strip in recent weeks. Two people were critically wounded in a shooting at a parking garage on February 6, and a tourist was stabbed in an elevator at The Hotel at Mandalay Bay on Saturday. Despite these incidents, police have assured tourists that the area is still safe and that they have made arrests or identified suspects in each case.\n\n**Reactions from Tourists**\n\nMany tourists were shocked and saddened by the incident, but some were more sanguine. \"I'm here for the day",
  "answers": [
    "Police in three states are still hunting for a Range Rover whose occupants opened fire on another car on the Vegas Strip this morning and set off a deadly chain reaction. Cops don't know most of the details, but they say it started with a dispute of some kind in one of the nearby hotels, then spilled into the street, reports the Las Vegas Sun. When the Range Rover caught up to a Maserati at a stop light, shots were fired from the SUV that sent the Maserati crashing into a taxi, which exploded upon impact. Three people—the Maserati driver, the taxi driver, and a taxi passenger—were killed, and three others were injured, reports the LA Times. Police are hoping to piece together more details by interviewing a passenger in the Maserati, who was injured in the melee. Earlier reports that gunfire came from both vehicles as part of a moving shootout were incorrect. The AP collects this quote from a tourist visiting from Manchester, England: \"This doesn't happen where we come from, not on this scale. We get stabbings, and gang violence, but this is like something out of a movie. Like Die Hard or something.\""
